4:29Z","email":"nenad@sols.mk","name":"Nenad Zafirovski"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-10-29T22:14:29Z","email":"nenad@sols.mk","name":"Nenad Zafirovski"},"message":"refactor: Slim down orchestration service from 1787 to 360 lines\n\nCompletes Phase 2 refactor by transforming the monolithic orchestration service into a thin orchestrator that delegates to the new modular services.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Reduced from 1787 lines → 360 lines (79% reduction)\n- Imports all 13 modular services from src/services/promidata/\n- Delegates all business logic to specialized services\n- Maintains backward compatibility with controller interface\n\n**Methods Refactored:**\n- startSync(): Orchestrates single or multi-supplier sync\n- syncSupplier(): Core sync flow with 4-step process\n  1. Parse Import.txt (variant URLs)\n  2. Fetch and group variants by a_number\n  3. Batch hash check on product families (Quick Win #2)\n  4. Process families needing sync\n- processProductFamily(): Creates Product + ProductVariants with primary flags\n- importCategories(): Delegates to category parser\n- getSyncStatus(): Returns sync status for all suppliers\n- getSyncHistory(): Returns paginated sync logs\n- testConnection(): Tests Promidata API connectivity\n\n**Architecture:**\n- Thin orchestration layer coordinates workflow\n- Business logic lives in modular services\n- Clean separation of concerns\n- Implements Product → ProductVariant hierarchy\n\nThis completes the modularization effort started in PR #7.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e9bc0c232be10ebc27ed4cd1a018575954860fc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neno73/PromovereAtlasPim/git/trees/e9bc0c232be10ebc27ed4cd1a018575954860fc8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Neno73/PromovereAtlasPim/git/commits/151d8cf43881876c10adcd1b27c8e798fbf27f56","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":fa